  *event = {touch_id = 0}; seat->touch_id = -1;
  seat->touch_state.touch_points empty (prev == next == head 0xaaaae0b78330).
  PhocCursorPrivate: drag_surface "phosh top-panel", DRAG_MODE_HANDLE,
  drag_handle 404, folded -708 / unfolded 0, state ANIMATING, anim_dir IN,
  anim_start 0 -> anim_end -708, anim_duration 300000, anim_t 0, margin.top 0.

  Reading: no drag was ever accepted (accept_drag writes
  layer_surface->current.margin.top directly; margin.top 0 / anim_start 0),
  including during the UPDATE that gesture.c emits on TOUCH_END before
  remove_point. anim_t == 0 means no frame since the slide started, so the
  slide began in this dispatch. A full-length IN slide with margin 0 comes from
  on_swipe -> phoc_draggable_layer_surface_fling() == TRUE -> send_touch_cancel
  -> wlr_seat_touch_notify_cancel -> touch_point_destroy -> free(point), inside
  TOUCH_END dispatch. phoc_cursor_handle_touch_up had fetched point before
  dispatch (cursor.c:1603) and dereferenced it at 1633.
  Trigger (inference): last updated point in the handle region plus
  |vy| >= 1500 px/s without an accepted drag. A <16 px flick is one candidate;
  a sideways-rejected drag followed by a fling is another. The core cannot
  tell them apart.

